<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.55 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
         margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; color: #16191d; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  p.what { color: #3d4451; }
  p.status { color: #3d4451; }
  p.stamp { color: #5b6270; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 0; }
  p.project { color: #5b6270; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  p.role-intro { margin-top: 2rem; }
  table.roles { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  table.roles th, table.roles td { text-align: left; padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem 0.35rem 0;
                                   border-bottom: 1px solid #d8dce3; vertical-align: top; }
  table.roles thead th { border-bottom: 1px solid #9aa1ad; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
  li p { margin: 0.1rem 0 0; color: #3d4451; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  code { font-size: 0.9em; }
  footer { border-top: 1px solid #d8dce3; margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 0.75rem;
           color: #5b6270; font-size: 0.85rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
<p class="what">{{ one_liner }}</p>
<p class="status">{{ status_line }}</p>
<p class="project"><a href="/">New to the project? What it is and how to access and use it: start at the project page.</a></p>
<p class="role-intro">{{ role_intro_html }}</p>
<table class="roles">
  <thead>
    <tr>{% for column in role_table_header %}<th>{{ column }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
{% for row in role_table_rows_html %}
    <tr>{% for cell in row %}<td>{{ cell }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<h2>Artifacts</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="catalogue.html">Catalogue (HTML)</a>
    <p>The full reference edition, with a table of contents and an anchor on
    every threat, control, fact and reference ID, so specifications can
    deep-link.</p></li>
  <li><a href="evidence-pack.html">Evidence pack</a>
    <p>One section per ID: its claim record, its references with tier, URL
    and snapshot status, and the change-log rows that mention it.</p></li>
  <li><a href="references.html">References</a>
    <p>Every cited source with its tier, link and citation reach
    (Appendix B, rendered).</p></li>
  <li>Downloads
    <p><a href="downloads/catalogue.pdf">catalogue.pdf</a> &middot;
    <a href="downloads/catalogue.docx">catalogue.docx</a> &middot;
    <a href="downloads/evidence-pack.md">evidence-pack.md</a></p></li>
  <li><a href="ai/llms.txt">AI-optimised edition</a>
    <p>{% for name in ai_files %}<a href="ai/{{ name }}">{{ name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} &middot;
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p></li>
  <li><a href="history.html">History and provenance</a>
    <p>Where the catalogue came from and what beta means
    (HISTORY.md, rendered).</p></li>
  <li><a href="{{ releases_url }}">GitHub releases</a>
    <p>Earlier versions of the catalogue, tagged and archived.</p></li>
</ul>
<footer>{{ stamp }}</footer>
</body>
</html>
